## Severity and disposition

Grade every finding:

- trivial — rounding, no effect on any conclusion. Disposition: note only.
- low — a single figure differs, no conclusion affected. Disposition: note; correction optional.
- medium — changes a supporting figure. Disposition: the calling pipeline corrects inline with attribution.
- high — changes the primary conclusion. Disposition: surface immediately; the pipeline must re-examine the conclusion.
- critical — invalidates a section. Disposition: surface immediately; the pipeline must withdraw the section.

Class defaults: W findings are trivial unless the quantity is load-bearing (then low). N findings are low, or medium when the difference is material and unresolved. E findings are medium by default, high when the corrected value changes the primary conclusion, critical when it invalidates the section. When you cannot tell whether a figure is load-bearing, say so in the `why` and grade down, not up — a graduated system that overcalls destroys its own signal.

## Instructions

1. Assign IDs in encounter order within each class: E1, E2...; W1...; N1...
2. Every entry carries `prior_value` (what the report stated). Class E entries also carry `corrected_value` (what the computation produced). Class N entries name both conflicting values with their sources and periods in the description — there is no single corrected value.
3. Every entry carries a `why` of at least 40 characters stating the materiality judgment.
4. The log is append-only: nothing is removed, reordered after assignment, or merged away.
5. Emit the totals.

## Output format

Produce a JSON object:

```json
{
  "error_log": [
    {
      "id": "E1",
      "class": "E",
      "claim_id": "claim_007",
      "description": "Bucket B P/S median averaged the wrong pair",
      "prior_value": "1.43x",
      "corrected_value": "1.29x",
      "severity": "medium",
      "disposition": "correct inline with attribution",
      "why": "The median feeds the peer-comparison table; the wrong pair shifts the bucket multiple but not the discount conclusion."
    }
  ],
  "totals": { "corrected": 1, "data_notes": 0, "warnings": 0 }
}
```
